From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: log a recovered radio without the warning rate limit

ath11k_warn() is dev_warn_ratelimited() with one rate limit (10 lines per
5 s) for every ath11k warning. When the firmware crashes, the commands in
flight fail with -108 and each logs a warning; on an RD03v2 (IPQ5018, a Q6
assert while hostapd was updating the beacon) eleven of them use up the
budget, and both radios recover within the next second with no "pdev 1
successfully recovered" in the log, and no "callbacks suppressed" line later
either, since no further warning comes.

The recovery itself is complete (the state goes back to ON and the queues
wake), but that line is how userspace tells an in-place recovery apart from a
radio left down: the RD03v2 watchdog rejoins an encrypted mesh on it.

Log it with dev_warn(), at the same level and with the same text, outside the
rate limit. It is printed once per radio per recovery.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -9566,8 +9566,13 @@ ath11k_mac_op_reconfig_complete(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	mutex_lock(&ar->conf_mutex);
 
 	if (ar->state == ATH11K_STATE_RESTARTED) {
-		ath11k_warn(ar->ab, "pdev %d successfully recovered\n",
-			    ar->pdev->pdev_id);
+		/* Not ath11k_warn(): its rate limit is shared with every other
+		 * warning, and the failed commands of the crash that led here
+		 * often use it up, dropping this line that tells a recovery
+		 * apart from a radio left down.
+		 */
+		dev_warn(ar->ab->dev, "pdev %d successfully recovered\n",
+			 ar->pdev->pdev_id);
 		ar->state = ATH11K_STATE_ON;
 		ieee80211_wake_queues(ar->hw);
 
